# 2026-06-10 15:11:02.851338
+In my Augmentra Unity 6 project, build a complete in-game HUD from scratch using Unity Canvas UI with TextMeshPro and Nexa Extra font. Dark and minimal style — dark semi-transparent backgrounds, small clean text, nothing flashy. Follow this exact layout:
+
+TOP BAR — stretched full width across the top of the screen:
+- Left side: HP bar, dark background, red or dark crimson fill, shows current/max HP numbers on top of the bar in Nexa Extra (e.g. "80 / 100"), thin and wide bar
+- Right side next to HP bar: Wave text in Nexa Extra showing "Wave 1", "Wave 2" etc, small and clean, white text
+- Top bar panel has a very subtle dark semi-transparent background
+
+BOTTOM CENTER — ability bar:
+- 4 square slots in a horizontal row centered at the bottom
+- Each slot is a dark panel with a rounded border, empty for now but ready to receive ability icons later
+- Below each slot a small keybind label: Q, W, E, R in Nexa Extra
+- Left of the ability bar: Gold display, small coin icon placeholder and gold amount text in Nexa Extra, gold colored text
+
+BOTTOM RIGHT — inventory:
+- 6 square slots in a 3x2 grid anchored to bottom right
+- Each slot dark background with a colored border glow that changes based on rarity: Common = grey, Rare = blue, Epic = purple, Legendary = gold
+- Slots empty by default, ready to receive item icons when items are purchased from shop
+- Small and compact, not taking too much screen space
+
+WAVE ANNOUNCEMENT — center screen:
+- When a new wave starts, show a large text in the center of the screen saying "Wave 1" then "Wave 2" etc in Nexa Extra font
+- Fades in quickly, stays for 2 seconds, fades out
+- Behind the text a very subtle dark vignette or panel
+- Completely disappears after fade out, does not block gameplay
+
+Create a HUDManager.cs script that:
+- Updates HP bar fill and text from the player health script
+- Updates wave number text and triggers wave announcement from WaveManager.cs
+- Updates gold display from the player gold script
+- Has public methods: UpdateHP(float current, float max), UpdateWave(int waveNumber), UpdateGold(int amount), AddItemToInventory(ItemSO item)
+
+All panels use dark colors: #0D0D0D or #111111 at 70-80% opacity. No bright colors except the HP bar fill and rarity glows. Nexa Extra font throughout. No comments, complete file replacements only, Unity 6 API.

